{
 "hash": "0ee46728a38166",
 "text": "The whistle blew. KD drove, drew all three defenders, and whipped the pass to me at the elbow. No lightning. No superpowers. Just months of muscle memory. I rose up for the pull-up middy. The buzzer went off with the ball in the air. Swish. We won by one. The entire arena exploded. KD lifted me onto his shoulders, and twenty thousand people chanted my name. The lightning gave me a head start—but the countless days and months in the gym made it real. The next day, back on my street, Dex won the coin toss to pick first. He looked at every kid on the court. Then he pointed straight at me.",
